# Sources and scope audit

## Original target

Volker Kaibel, *Open Problem: Arborescences and NP-hardness*, Oberwolfach Report50/2018, printed pp.3014–3015, Problem2. [Official complete report](https://ems.press/content/serial-article-files/46772). The entire short contribution was read; printed p.3015 was visually checked. The input is an arbitrary directed graph, fixed root and one real arc-cost vector per nonroot destination. The objective adds each destination's own costs along its root path. The source motivates it through Wong's extended formulation.

Problem1 on the preceding page instead uses an undirected spanning tree and aggregates all rooted orientations, motivated by Martin's formulation. These are separately numbered source targets. The dataset assessment for30003997 mistakenly describes the first problem in one background sentence; the full original statement, displayed formula and corrected record identify Problem2 unambiguously.

## Classical NP-complete source problem

Richard M. Karp, *Reducibility among Combinatorial Problems*, in Complexity of Computer Computations (1972),85–103. [DOI](https://doi.org/10.1007/978-1-4684-2001-2_9); [full primary scan hosted by George Washington University](https://www2.seas.gwu.edu/~simhaweb/champalg/tsp/papers/KarpOriginal.pdf). The full19-page scan was obtained. The theorem/list and printed p.95 item11 identify satisfiability with at most three literals per clause. The proof here relies on this classical NP-completeness theorem and supplies its own reduction to the exact arborescence problem.

The cs170 and older Berkeley candidate PDF endpoints returned HTML; those files are not mathematical sources and are excluded from the manifest.

## Prior-attempt and duplicate gate

The current queued0/5 row, repository and queue instructions, full pinned record, no-join result from the research-report dictionary, related-target metadata, all-ref selected-path history and remote branch names were checked.100 all-state PRs had no attempt matching30003997 or its duplicate30003998. There was no prior attempted folder in the fresh main checkout. Record30003998 explicitly repeats the same source Problem2 and is not a second target.

The concurrent Problem1 /30003996 research uses a closely related assignment-and-literal-witness mechanism. The present proof was formulated directly for the layered directed graph and does not invoke a transfer from that model. The shared idea is credited in PROOF.md; no two unrelated conceptual discoveries or model equivalence are asserted.

A bounded current search used the exact report/question, Kaibel with Wong and integer optimization, destination-dependent path costs and arborescence hardness. It did not verify a prior proof of this exact restricted statement. Ordinary minimum arborescences, minimax-regret costs, changeover/reload costs and quadratic local path costs have different objectives and were not substituted. This search does not establish novelty.
